# openElement Showcase

Generated by [`@openelement/create`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@openelement/create) —
a static-first openElement app that shows its own costs. The landing page
carries two islands (`my-counter`, an interactive counter, and `live-timer`,
a client-only elapsed-time readout); every other page, including `/about`,
is prerendered HTML and CSS with no islands at all. The badge on each
section names what it costs the client.

Docs and guides: https://openelement.org

One directory is generated rather than source: `.openElement/` at the project
root holds the build's internal state (head-convention bookkeeping and build
plans). `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build` write it as needed; the `.gitignore`
excludes it and deleting it is safe — the next run recreates it.

This starter pins the exact `@openelement/element` and `@openelement/router`
versions it was generated from in `package.json`; update both there when
moving to a new release.

## The JS cost map

| Surface | Ships JavaScript? | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/` hero + architecture sections | no | prerendered markup, styled with CSS |
| `/` counter island (`my-counter`) | yes, hydrates on idle | the one interactive piece |
| `/` live timer island (`live-timer`) | yes, client-only | a live clock has nothing to prerender |
| `/about` | no islands at all | fully static SSG output |
| `/api/ping` | no (server) | a plain `Request → Response` handler |

The badge classes (`badge-static`, `badge-island`) live in
`app/components/page-styles.ts` — copy them onto new sections and keep the
map honest.

> Cost honesty: the island client is emitted app-wide today. A page without
> islands (like `/about`) carries no island hosts and renders nothing
> interactive, but the shared loader — and with the current app-wide
> hydration manifest, the island chunks themselves — still ride along in its
> network panel. Per-page pruning is framework work, not something a template
> can opt into; the page is authored so it becomes fully silent the moment
> the framework ships it.

## Where things live

Framework options have exactly one home: `openelement.config.ts`. It is
optional and nearly empty — every option it omits comes from a file
convention:

| Option | Convention |
| --- | --- |
| design tokens | `app/styles/tokens.css` |
| document head content | `app/head.tsx` (meta tags, preloads, inline CSS) |
| site title | the `name` field of `package.json` |

Passing framework options inline to `openElement()` while the config file
carries options is a hard error, and an unknown key fails the build with the
accepted-key list. `vite.config.ts` stays Vite-only: `plugins: [...openElement()]`.

- `app/routes/` — page routes, one file per URL. The default renderIntent is
  `static`: prerendered at build time (SSG). `/about` and `/` are static.
- `app/routes/api/` — request-time server routes. `/api/ping` is a plain
  WinterCG-shaped handler returning `Response.json`.
- `app/components/` — compiled page elements and their style sheets
  (`page-styles.ts` is the single home of page CSS; each page spreads the
  shared chrome sheet).
- `app/islands/` — client islands, the only code that ships JavaScript. Each
  island declares its hydration strategy (`idle`, `load`, `visible`,
  client-only) through `defineIslandConfig`.
- `app/styles/tokens.css` — design tokens inlined into every document head.
  Dark values ride `prefers-color-scheme`; no theme runtime.
- `app/head.tsx` — structural head content the URL list cannot express.

## Scripts

- `pnpm dev` — start the Vite dev server.
- `pnpm check` — type-check every route/component file. The check covers the
  whole `app/` directory (`tsconfig.json`), so new files are picked up
  automatically.
- `pnpm test` — run Node's built-in test runner (the starter ships none).
- `pnpm build` — production build (SSG + Nitro server) into `dist/`.
- `pnpm start` — serve the production build.
- `pnpm preview` — static-only preview of the SSG output.

## Styling ownership

Global design tokens and the document baseline (`body`, `::selection`) live
in `app/styles/tokens.css`. Pages use light roots and own their rules in
`static styles` (`app/components/page-styles.ts`): the server inlines each
page's sheets into the SSR output as a `@scope(<page-tag>)` style block, so
pages are fully styled with zero client JavaScript. Islands carry their own
same-module `compiledStyle()` sheets.

## Brand assets

`public/openelement-mark.svg` is the openElement brand mark shipped with the
starter — the config file references it as the favicon, or delete it if
unused.

## Dependency notes

`hono` and `@hono/vite-dev-server` are installed even though no source file
imports them: the dev server resolves `hono` when loading the generated
server entry (the bundled `dist/` output inlines it). For Nitro deployments,
the built handler bridges through the `@openelement/router/nitro-mount`
subpath of the one `@openelement/router` dependency. Do not remove them.
